p other  people's lives  but also offer you deep satisfaction  strategize seek and build excellence  build operational excellence around your  idea put together a solid business model  that you feel proud of and that meets a  need  addressing not only the return on the  investment but also  the social return on investment  and finally implement use the vast  resources  that are available right here at mit and  across boston  there will be workshops and programs  designed to help you  build and amplify your adventure so you  can bring your creative vision  into the spotlight take advantage of all  of it  as you will carry these skills with you  for the rest of your life  throughout the entire process we remind  you  to remember the values of being thinking  like an artist  remember the power of improvisation  empathy  social imagination and resourcefulness  in her book the culture of possibility  arlene goldbard  writes we need to learn to see like the  most committed and skilled artists  eyes wide open taking it all in turning  away from nothing  cultivating empathy and imagination  taking risks admitting mistakes and  persevering  in essence my friends the arts and  entrepreneurship  are really not that different both rely  on storytelling to express  compelling narratives both are about  taking risks  and making mistakes and persevering  whatever your entrepreneurial journey is  and whatever story got you here today  we are here to say yes go for it  you've got this there is so much hope  and potential and opportunity at the  intersection  of arts and technology and the 15k  creative arts competition is the perfect  launching pad for you  we commend you as you set forth on your  journey and we look forward to seeing  the seeds that you plant today and see  how they grow over the course of the  months ahead  your work will help to reimagine the  jobs the products  and the services of the future  thank you for joining us and thank you  arts at mit  for inviting crea